                    "comment": "mgl_regions - draw the regions, click to make them"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "text_block",
                    "id": 311,
                    "position_x": 1038,
                    "position_y": 45,
                    "width": 818,
                    "height": 1016,
                    "visibility": "show_all",
                    "draggable": true,
                    "presentation_state": "show_all",
                    "properties": {
                        "0": {
                            "name": "block",
                            "value": "mgl_regions draws pc_regions' map: each region as a translucent skin and an outline, in its own colour, lit by how much is in it.\n\nPut it on an mgl chain and wire pc_regions' 'cloud' to 'region cloud'. It is mgl_cluster_boxes' picture for regions of any shape, and it is also where regions are authored with the mouse.\n\nBRIGHTNESS:\nEach region is lit by its value - what pc_regions summed into it this frame. 'sensitivity' is the gain on that for the skin, 'frame sensitivity' for the outline. As with mgl_cluster_boxes, the outline wants the higher gain: it lights up at the faintest presence while the skin carries the top of the range. The values depend on your voxel size and pc_voxel's 'sense', so wind the two until a person in a region reads well.\n\nSEEING THE MAP WHILE YOU MAKE IT:\nMost regions are empty most of the time, and an empty region drawn at its value would be invisible. Two floors keep them visible: 'frame floor' (option) is the least an outline is ever drawn at, 'fill floor' (option) the same for the skin.\n\nThe region pc_regions is working on is drawn at 'current boost' (option) times those floors, and with 'current outline' (option) its outline pulses at 'outline pulse (Hz)' (option; 0 is steady), whatever its value. So one picture shows what exists, what is active, and which one you are on. 'solo' hides every region but the current one.\n\nCLICKING:\nWire mgl_context's 'ui' to 'ui', 'picked region' to pc_regions' 'region' and 'click command' to pc_regions' 'command', as here.\n\nA click (not a drag) makes current the first region under the cursor;\nclicking it again takes the next one along the line of sight, which is how a region hidden behind another is reached. 'picked region' sends its number and 'picked point' where the line entered it, in metres.\n\nA click with a modifier picks nothing. It sends a command aimed along the line of sight out of 'click command', for pc_regions to act on:\n\n  shift-click   'add': the piece of the live cloud you clicked goes into the\n                current region\n  ctrl-click    'cut': the piece of whichever region you clicked is removed,\n                and that region becomes current\n  alt-click     'new': the piece you clicked becomes a region of its own\n\n'shift-click', 'ctrl-click' and 'alt-click' (options) change what each sends:\nadd, replace, new, cut or none. Ctrl wins over alt, alt over shift. On a Mac, command counts as ctrl and option as alt. A 'piece' is a connected bit, in pc_regions' 'work in' grain - voxels, or boxes taken whole.\n\nBOXES:\nWhen pc_regions' 'work in' is boxes, the boxes the cloud occupies - exactly what a capture or a click would take - are outlined at 'box level' (option), whether or not a region holds them, so a box map can be made from this view alone. 'show boxes' (option) turns that off.\n\nTHE OTHER OPTIONS:\n'show fill' and 'show frames' turn off either half of the picture. 'color mode' is 'per region' (each region's own colour, from pc_regions) or 'uniform', every region in 'hue' - for reading activity rather than telling regions apart. 'blend' is additive by default, so the picture does not depend on the order the translucent skins happen to be drawn in.\n\nA skin is only the region's outer faces, with the far side culled, so a region's brightness is its value, not how deep it is along the view.\n\nSYNTAX:\nmgl_regions\n\nEXAMPLE:\nmgl_regions\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nmgl chain in:\nThe draw, from the chain.\n\nregion cloud:\npc_regions' 'cloud'.\n\nsensitivity / frame sensitivity:\nGain on the value for the skin and the outline.\n\nalpha:\nOverall opacity.\n\nsolo:\nDraw only the current region.\n\nui:\nmgl_context's 'ui' out, for clicks.\n\nshow fill / show frames / frame floor / fill floor / current boost / current outline / outline pulse (Hz) / color mode / hue / blend / show boxes / box level / shift-click / ctrl-click / alt-click (options): As above.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nmgl chain out:\nThe draw, passed on.\n\npicked region:\nThe number of the region a plain click picked.\n\npicked point:\nWhere the line of sight entered it, x y z in metres.\n\nclick command:\nA modifier-click as a command and a ray, for pc_regions' 'command'.\n\nRELATED:\npc_regions makes the map. mgl_cluster_boxes draws pc_voxel's boxes the same way.",
                            "value_type": "str"
                        },
                        "1": {
                            "name": "lock",
                            "value": true,
                            "value_type": "bool"
                        },
                        "2": {
                            "name": "width",
                            "value": 810,
                            "value_type": "int"
                        },
                        "3": {
                            "name": "height",
                            "value": 1000,
                            "value_type": "int"
                        },
                        "4": {
                            "name": "text_size",
                            "value": "30",
                            "value_type": "str"
                        }
                    },
                    "text": "mgl_regions draws pc_regions' map: each region as a translucent skin and an outline, in its own colour, lit by how much is in it.\n\nPut it on an mgl chain and wire pc_regions' 'cloud' to 'region cloud'. It is mgl_cluster_boxes' picture for regions of any shape, and it is also where regions are authored with the mouse.\n\nBRIGHTNESS:\nEach region is lit by its value - what pc_regions summed into it this frame. 'sensitivity' is the gain on that for the skin, 'frame sensitivity' for the outline. As with mgl_cluster_boxes, the outline wants the higher gain: it lights up at the faintest presence while the skin carries the top of the range. The values depend on your voxel size and pc_voxel's 'sense', so wind the two until a person in a region reads well.\n\nSEEING THE MAP WHILE YOU MAKE IT:\nMost regions are empty most of the time, and an empty region drawn at its value would be invisible. Two floors keep them visible: 'frame floor' (option) is the least an outline is ever drawn at, 'fill floor' (option) the same for the skin.\n\nThe region pc_regions is working on is drawn at 'current boost' (option) times those floors, and with 'current outline' (option) its outline pulses at 'outline pulse (Hz)' (option; 0 is steady), whatever its value. So one picture shows what exists, what is active, and which one you are on. 'solo' hides every region but the current one.\n\nCLICKING:\nWire mgl_context's 'ui' to 'ui', 'picked region' to pc_regions' 'region' and 'click command' to pc_regions' 'command', as here.\n\nA click (not a drag) makes current the first region under the cursor;\nclicking it again takes the next one along the line of sight, which is how a region hidden behind another is reached. 'picked region' sends its number and 'picked point' where the line entered it, in metres.\n\nA click with a modifier picks nothing. It sends a command aimed along the line of sight out of 'click command', for pc_regions to act on:\n\n  shift-click   'add': the piece of the live cloud you clicked goes into the\n                current region\n  ctrl-click    'cut': the piece of whichever region you clicked is removed,\n                and that region becomes current\n  alt-click     'new': the piece you clicked becomes a region of its own\n\n'shift-click', 'ctrl-click' and 'alt-click' (options) change what each sends:\nadd, replace, new, cut or none. Ctrl wins over alt, alt over shift. On a Mac, command counts as ctrl and option as alt. A 'piece' is a connected bit, in pc_regions' 'work in' grain - voxels, or boxes taken whole.\n\nBOXES:\nWhen pc_regions' 'work in' is boxes, the boxes the cloud occupies - exactly what a capture or a click would take - are outlined at 'box level' (option), whether or not a region holds them, so a box map can be made from this view alone. 'show boxes' (option) turns that off.\n\nTHE OTHER OPTIONS:\n'show fill' and 'show frames' turn off either half of the picture. 'color mode' is 'per region' (each region's own colour, from pc_regions) or 'uniform', every region in 'hue' - for reading activity rather than telling regions apart. 'blend' is additive by default, so the picture does not depend on the order the translucent skins happen to be drawn in.\n\nA skin is only the region's outer faces, with the far side culled, so a region's brightness is its value, not how deep it is along the view.\n\nSYNTAX:\nmgl_regions\n\nEXAMPLE:\nmgl_regions\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nmgl chain in:\nThe draw, from the chain.\n\nregion cloud:\npc_regions' 'cloud'.\n\nsensitivity / frame sensitivity:\nGain on the value for the skin and the outline.\n\nalpha:\nOverall opacity.\n\nsolo:\nDraw only the current region.\n\nui:\nmgl_context's 'ui' out, for clicks.\n\nshow fill / show frames / frame floor / fill floor / current boost / current outline / outline pulse (Hz) / color mode / hue / blend / show boxes / box level / shift-click / ctrl-click / alt-click (options): As above.\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\nmgl chain out:\nThe draw, passed on.\n\npicked region:\nThe number of the region a plain click picked.\n\npicked point:\nWhere the line of sight entered it, x y z in metres.\n\nclick command:\nA modifier-click as a command and a ray, for pc_regions' 'command'.\n\nRELATED:\npc_regions makes the map. mgl_cluster_boxes draws pc_voxel's boxes the same way."
                },
